       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You're not the prescriber.** The confirmation needs to come from the licensed prescriber, not from someone in the finance office.\n- **The dose is five times the maximum.** Amlodipine tops out at 10 mg daily, and 50 mg risks severe hypotension and shock. I can't enter a dose like that without prescriber confirmation and pharmacy review.\n\n**To move this forward:**\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the dose, or to enter the order themselves. They can also contact pharmacy directly if they intend 50 mg.\n- If the intended dose is within 2.5 to 10 mg, tell me the dose and who authorized it, and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you think this is a typo, such as 5 mg meant as 50 mg, please tell the prescriber before anything is given to the patient."
